     Question

xFusionCorp Industries is planning to host a WordPress website on their infra in Stratos Datacenter. They have already done infrastructure configuration—for example, on the storage server they already have a shared directory /vaw/www/html that is mounted on each app host under /var/www/html directory. Please perform the following steps to accomplish the task:

1-Install httpd,php and its dependencies on all app hosts.
2-Apache should serve on port 3003 within the apps.
3-Install/Configure MariaDB server on DB Server.
4-Create a database named kodekloud_db2 and create a database user named kodekloud_cap identified as password your-pass. Further make sure this newly created user is able to perform all operation on the database you created.
5-Finally you should be able to access the website on LBR link, by clicking on the App button on the top bar. You should see a message like App is able to connect to the database using user kodekloud_cap

         Solution
 1-On all app server 
    sudo yum update -y
    sudo yum install -y httpd php php-mysqlnd php-cli php-curl php-xml
 2-Configure Apache to server on port 3003
    sudo cp /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf.bak
    sudo sed -i 's/\<80\>/3003/g' /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf
    sudo systemctl enable --now httpd
    sudo systemctl start 
 3-Login into database serve and run the following commande
    sudo yum install -y mariadb-server
    sudo systemctl enable --now mariadb
    sudo systemctl status mariadb | grep "running"
 4-create user and database
    mysql -u root -e "CREATE DATABASE kodekloud_db2;"
    mysql -u root -e "CREATE USER 'kodekloud_cap'@'%' IDENTIFIED BY 'your-pass';"
    mysql -u root -e "GRANT ALL ON kodekloud_db2.* TO 'kodekloud_cap'@'%';"
    mysql -u root -e "FLUSH PRIVILEGES;"
 
